Subject: [PATCH] target/m68k: set the 68040 M bit on the first write after a read

A table search made for a read loaded the TLB entry writable even while
the page descriptor's M bit was clear, so a later write hit that entry
and M was never set.  Guests that track dirty pages through M then lose
the write at pageout or sync.

The MC68040 sets M before the first write to a page: a write that hits
an ATC entry with M clear searches the table again to set M (M68040
User's Manual, 3.5 Address Translation Summary).  Map such a page
read-only after a read so the first write takes the store path.

--- a/target/m68k/helper.c
+++ b/target/m68k/helper.c
@@ -892,6 +892,13 @@
                 goto txfail;
             }
         }
+        /*
+         * The first write through an entry with M clear must search the
+         * table again to set M, so a read does not map the page writable.
+         */
+        if (!(next & M68K_DESC_MODIFIED)) {
+            *prot &= ~PAGE_WRITE;
+        }
     }
 
     if (env->mmu.tcr & M68K_TCR_PAGE_8K) {
